            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of dural arteriovenous fistulas presenting as pulsatile tinnitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>897-902</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/MAO.0b013e3181b76aef</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe the clinical picture and treatment of dural arteriovenous fistulas (DAVFs) presenting as pulsatile subjective tinnitus.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Review of prospectively collected data.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">Academic referral center.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Fourteen patients with clinically and radiographically diagnosed DAVFs.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Treated by endovascular route.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES" NlmCategory="METHODS">Treatments, clinical course, complications, and evolution were evaluated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">All patients presented with sleep-disruptive pulsatile tinnitus. Other symptoms included severe headaches, papilledema, proptosis, blepharoptosis, visual disturbances, and hemiparesis. Cortical venous drainage was present in 4 cases. Endovascular treatment was performed at least once by the arterial route in 14 patients and the venous route in 4 patients. The origin of tinnitus was always a vessel in or above the petrous bone. When these arteries or veins could not be visualized in the final control, the tinnitus disappeared. In the patients whose tinnitus returned, a vessel in the petrous bone could always be seen. There was no mortality.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Endovascular treatment is an effective and safe treatment of DAVFs presenting as tinnitus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
